  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31404384",
      "title": "Configuring the Form Input Elements",
      "lectureOrder": 149,
      "videoOrder": 145,
      "sourceHash": "8ff53f88feb53dc53cbe5adcd279920023bad26aca3b2b873c57c43a74809d54",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 4.27,
          "en": "Which kind of configuration could we add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.27,
          "end": 6.43,
          "en": "to this description?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.43,
          "end": 8.39,
          "en": "We could set the keyboardType",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.39,
          "end": 10.67,
          "en": "but actually I'm fine with the default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.67,
          "end": 13.93,
          "en": "because the description should allow all kinds of characters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.93,
          "end": 16.03,
          "en": "so opening that default keyboard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.03,
          "end": 18.4,
          "en": "which makes entering text very easy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.4,
          "end": 20.46,
          "en": "sounds like a good idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.46,
          "end": 24.94,
          "en": "But there is one other key property that I do wanna set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.94,
          "end": 26.64,
          "en": "And that's the multiline property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.095,
          "end": 31.37,
          "en": "Multiline is a prop supported on text input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.37,
          "end": 34.13,
          "en": "and multiline does what the name suggests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.13,
          "end": 37.9,
          "en": "It allows users to enter multiple lines of text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.9,
          "end": 41.46,
          "en": "or to be precise, it makes that a bit easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.46,
          "end": 44.33,
          "en": "On Android, we could then also add number of lines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.33,
          "end": 47.9,
          "en": "to restrict how many lines can be entered basically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.9,
          "end": 49.52,
          "en": "Though, I don't wanna add that here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.52,
          "end": 52.72,
          "en": "but you could add this prop in addition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.72,
          "end": 55.53,
          "en": "But it's not just multiline which I wanna add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.53,
          "end": 57.04,
          "en": "and which I wanna set to true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.04,
          "end": 60.71,
          "en": "to turn this into a multiline text input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.71,
          "end": 64.693,
          "en": "but I also wanna talk about some auto correction props here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.73,
          "end": 69.99,
          "en": "To be precise, we got autoCapitalize and autoCorrect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.99,
          "end": 71.7,
          "en": "And these can be very useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.7,
          "end": 74.2,
          "en": "but also very annoying props as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.2,
          "end": 77.07,
          "en": "At least they can be annoying if you don't know them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.07,
          "end": 81.64,
          "en": "Because by default, for example, autoCorrect is set to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.64,
          "end": 83.41,
          "en": "Now when having a text input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.41,
          "end": 86.72,
          "en": "where users enter text, this can be annoying.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.72,
          "end": 88.53999999999999,
          "en": "For example, if you're building an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.53999999999999,
          "end": 90.57,
          "en": "for entering email addresses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.57,
          "end": 93.89,
          "en": "in that case you don't wanna have auto correction turned on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.89,
          "end": 97.59,
          "en": "because we probably all know those text input fields",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.59,
          "end": 100.53999999999999,
          "en": "where we have to enter a email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.53999999999999,
          "end": 103.45,
          "en": "where it keeps correcting our email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.45,
          "end": 104.87,
          "en": "whilst we're entering it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.87,
          "end": 108.61,
          "en": "It's super annoying and can lead to a lot of errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.61,
          "end": 111.56,
          "en": "But here for the description here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.56,
          "end": 115.09,
          "en": "it actually makes sense to add auto correction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.09,
          "end": 117.53,
          "en": "and to ensure that users are corrected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.53,
          "end": 120.4,
          "en": "and that we have some nice input here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.4,
          "end": 123.11,
          "en": "or at least that is my opinion for this app here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.11,
          "end": 127.63,
          "en": "You could turn it off by simply setting autoCorrect here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.63,
          "end": 128.623,
          "en": "to false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.73,
          "end": 133.9,
          "en": "The default is true and therefore doesn't need to be set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.9,
          "end": 135.31,
          "en": "Here, I will comment it out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.31,
          "end": 137.17000000000002,
          "en": "because I wanna keep that default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 137.17000000000002,
          "end": 140.79,
          "en": "but you could turn it off by setting it to false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 140.79,
          "end": 144.103,
          "en": "Though, it's autoCorrect with a capital C, that's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.16,
          "end": 147.23,
          "en": "We also have autoCapitalize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 147.23,
          "end": 148.92000000000002,
          "en": "which can also be annoying if we're,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 148.92000000000002,
          "end": 153.72,
          "en": "for example, dealing with email addresses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 153.72,
          "end": 155.12,
          "en": "but here you could control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 155.12,
          "end": 160.12,
          "en": "if the input entered by the user should be auto capitalized.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 160.19,
          "end": 163.31,
          "en": "And you actually don't set this to true or false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.31,
          "end": 166.57,
          "en": "but instead autoCapitalize wants a string value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 166.57,
          "end": 169.45,
          "en": "where you use one of these values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 169.45,
          "end": 173.38,
          "en": "to control whatever characters should be auto capitalized,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 173.38,
          "end": 175.77,
          "en": "entire words or just sentences.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.77,
          "end": 179.68,
          "en": "And sentences, as you can see, is the default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 179.68,
          "end": 181.81,
          "en": "Now here, I wanna stick to that default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 181.81,
          "end": 185,
          "en": "and ensure that sentences are auto capitalized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185,
          "end": 186.89,
          "en": "but you could control this as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 186.89,
          "end": 191.763,
          "en": "by setting the autoCapitalize prop here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.21,
          "end": 196.02,
          "en": "And then on this autoCapitalize prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.02,
          "end": 200.73,
          "en": "you, as mentioned, could set this to characters or words",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 200.73,
          "end": 202.88,
          "en": "or sentences, which is the default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 202.88,
          "end": 205.56,
          "en": "or none if you want to turn it off.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 205.56,
          "end": 208.75,
          "en": "But here, I'll keep it set to the default of sentences",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 208.75,
          "end": 210.623,
          "en": "but you could change it of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 211.93,
          "end": 213.21,
          "en": "And that's it for me",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 213.21,
          "end": 215.74,
          "en": "and the description input for the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 215.74,
          "end": 217.49,
          "en": "So actually there is only one piece",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 217.49,
          "end": 219.48,
          "en": "of configuration I wanna add here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 219.48,
          "end": 222.11,
          "en": "but I did wanna talk about autoCapitalize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 222.11,
          "end": 223.52,
          "en": "and autoCorrect as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 223.52,
          "end": 226.61,
          "en": "because these are all the very important props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 226.61,
          "end": 227.76,
          "en": "which you should know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 227.76,
          "end": 231.19,
          "en": "in order to configure your inputs correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 231.19,
          "end": 233.79,
          "en": "And with that, we added a bunch of inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 233.79,
          "end": 236.64,
          "en": "with some basic configuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 236.64,
          "end": 240.03,
          "en": "Now, as a next step, let's explore how we can style them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 240.03,
